# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill the values below.
# Vite picks up every `VITE_*` variable at build time and inlines it into
# the bundle. These ARE shipped to the client - never put a secret here.

# PayPal client-id override.
#
# By default the website ships with the jQWidgets live PayPal client-id
# baked into `src/lib/paypal.ts` (same account that backs htmlelements.com
# checkout). Real subscriptions work out of the box, no env config needed.
#
# Override only when you want a different account or want to disable
# checkout:
#   - any other PayPal client-id (sandbox or live) → swaps the merchant
#   - the literal value "sb" → disables checkout, shows "Contact sales"
#
# The client-id is a PUBLIC credential by design (PayPal calls it that);
# it identifies the merchant, not your account password.
#
# Sandbox client-ids: https://developer.paypal.com (Apps & Credentials → Sandbox)
# Live client-ids:    https://developer.paypal.com (Apps & Credentials → Live)
#VITE_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics via Umami (src/lib/analytics.ts)
#
# OFF by default: with no VITE_ANALYTICS_WEBSITE_ID set, the site loads NO
# script and sends nothing. Set the website id to switch it on. Analytics also
# self-disables when the visitor sends a Do Not Track / Global Privacy Control
# signal. The sv-grid library itself stays zero-telemetry regardless.
#
# These are PUBLIC values (a website id + a script URL), not secrets - set them
# in your GitHub Actions build step so they're baked into the deployed site.
#
# 1) Your Umami website id (a UUID). Create a site in Umami Cloud's free tier
#    (https://cloud.umami.is) and copy the id from Settings -> Websites:
#VITE_ANALYTICS_WEBSITE_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#
# 2) (optional) Tracker script URL. Defaults to Umami Cloud. Point this at a
#    self-hosted Umami instance later if you ever move off the free tier:
#VITE_ANALYTICS_SRC=https://cloud.umami.is/script.js
#
# 3) (optional) Override where events are sent (self-hosted/proxied only):
#VITE_ANALYTICS_HOST_URL=https://analytics.example.com
